#: ../../../user/hardware/certified-hardware/insurgo-privacybeast-x230.rst:16
#: 427cb42399de44ca8c07df9db4de76c1
msgid ""
"The `Insurgo PrivacyBeast X230 <https://insurgo.ca/produit/qubesos-certified-"
"privacybeast_x230-reasonably-secured-laptop/>`__ is a custom refurbished "
"`ThinkPad X230 <https://www.thinkwiki.org/wiki/Category:X230>`__ that "
"includes the following features:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/certified-hardware/insurgo-privacybeast-x230.rst:18
#: 02be68b671db4e9aa86691d8a959d005
msgid ""
"`coreboot <https://www.coreboot.org/>`__ initialization for the x230 is "
"binary-blob-free, including native graphic initialization. Built with the "
"`Heads <https://github.com/osresearch/heads/>`__ payload, it delivers "
"an :doc:`Anti Evil Maid (AEM) </user/security-in-qubes/anti-evil-maid>`-like "
"solution built into the firmware. (Even though our :ref:`requirements <user/"
"hardware/certified-hardware/certified-hardware:hardware certification "
"requirements>` provide an exception for CPU-vendor-provided blobs for "
"silicon and memory initialization, Insurgo exceeds our requirements by "
"insisting that these be absent from its machines.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/certified-hardware/insurgo-privacybeast-x230.rst:20
#: 4a2e9fe8732b4fa498049466fedae519
msgid ""
"`Intel ME <https://libreboot.org/faq.html#intelme>`__ is neutered through "
"the AltMeDisable bit, while all modules other than ROMP and BUP, which are "
"required to initialize main CPU, have been `deleted <https://github.com/"
"linuxboot/heads-wiki/blob/master/Installing-and-Configuring/Flashing-Guides/"
"Clean-the-ME-firmware.md#how-to-disabledeactive-most-of-it>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/certified-hardware/insurgo-privacybeast-x230.rst:22
#: 92a9dc02f30146e08046a80c1942c5ae
msgid ""
"A re-ownership process that allows it to ship pre-installed with Qubes OS, "
"including full-disk encryption already in place, but where the final disk "
"encryption key is regenerated only when the machine is first powered on by "
"the user, so that the OEM doesn’t know it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/certified-hardware/insurgo-privacybeast-x230.rst:24
#: 00348d6d0c5a4849979a835815d22dcb
msgid ""
"`Heads <https://github.com/osresearch/heads/>`__ provisioned pre-delivery to "
"protect against malicious `interdiction <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Interdiction>`__."
msgstr ""
